{"id":"mahabharata-4-021","work":"mahabharata","part":4,"partName":"विराटपर्व","partNameEn":"Virata Parva","unit":21,"title":"एकविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 21 · Bhima kills Kichaka","summary":{"en":"Bhima tells Draupadi to arrange to meet Kichaka that night in the dancing hall, which is empty after dark. Kichaka comes eagerly and finds Bhima waiting in the dark; they wrestle fiercely, and Bhima crushes him, pounding his limbs into his body until he is a shapeless ball of flesh.","kn":"ರಾತ್ರಿ ಖಾಲಿಯಿರುವ ನೃತ್ಯಶಾಲೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ಕೀಚಕನನ್ನು ಭೇಟಿಯಾಗಲು ಏರ್ಪಡಿಸೆಂದು ಭೀಮನು ದ್ರೌಪದಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಉತ್ಸಾಹದಿಂದ ಬಂದ ಕೀಚಕನು ಕತ್ತಲಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾದಿದ್ದ ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ಎದುರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಕರವಾಗಿ ಮಲ್ಲಯುದ್ಧ ಮಾಡಿ ಭೀಮನು ಅವನ ಅಂಗಗಳನ್ನು ದೇಹದೊಳಗೆ ತುರುಕಿ ಆಕಾರವಿಲ್ಲದ ಮಾಂಸಮುದ್ದೆಯನ್ನಾಗಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीम द्रौपदी से कहते हैं कि उस रात नृत्यशाला में कीचक से मिलने का प्रबन्ध करें, जो अँधेरे के बाद सूनी रहती है। कीचक उत्सुकता से आता है और अँधेरे में प्रतीक्षा करते भीम को पाता है; दोनों भयंकर कुश्ती लड़ते हैं, और भीम उसके अंगों को शरीर में ठूँसकर उसे मांस का आकारहीन लोथड़ा बना देते हैं।","te":"రాత్రి ఖాళీగా ఉండే నాట్యశాలలో కీచకుని కలిసేలా ఏర్పాటు చేయమని భీముడు ద్రౌపదికి చెబుతాడు. ఉత్సాహంగా వచ్చిన కీచకుడు చీకటిలో వేచి ఉన్న భీముని ఎదుర్కొంటాడు; భీకరంగా మల్లయుద్ధం చేసి భీముడు అతని అవయవాలను శరీరంలోకి దూర్చి ఆకారం లేని మాంసపు ముద్దగా చేస్తాడు.","ta":"இருட்டிய பின் வெறிச்சோடும் நடன மண்டபத்தில் அன்றிரவு கீசகனைச் சந்திக்க ஏற்பாடு செய்யுமாறு பீமன் திரௌபதியிடம் சொல்கிறான். ஆவலுடன் வந்த கீசகன் இருளில் காத்திருந்த பீமனைச் சந்திக்க, இருவரும் கடுமையாக மல்யுத்தம் செய்ய, பீமன் அவன் உறுப்புகளை உடலுக்குள் திணித்து வடிவற்ற சதைப் பிண்டமாக்குகிறான்.","ml":"രാത്രിയിൽ ആളൊഴിഞ്ഞ നൃത്തശാലയിൽ കീചകനെ കാണാൻ ഏർപ്പാടാക്കാൻ ഭീമൻ ദ്രൗപദിയോട് പറയുന്നു. ആവേശത്തോടെ എത്തിയ കീചകൻ ഇരുട്ടിൽ കാത്തിരിക്കുന്ന ഭീമനെ കാണുന്നു; ഇരുവരും കഠിനമായി ഗുസ്തി പിടിക്കുന്നു. ഭീമൻ അവന്റെ അവയവങ്ങൾ ശരീരത്തിലേക്ക് ഇടിച്ചമർത്തി, രൂപമില്ലാത്ത മാംസപിണ്ഡമാക്കി കൊല്ലുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 4.21; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Dec  1 2011","sections":[{"title":"कीचकवधपर्व","titleEn":"Kichakavadha Parva (Slaying of Kichaka)","verses":[{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तथा भद्रे करिष्यामि यथा त्वं भीरु भाषसे ।\nअद्य तं सूदयिष्यामि कीचकं सहबान्धवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall do as you say, timid lady; today I shall destroy Kichaka together with his kinsmen."}},{"n":2,"text":"अस्याः प्रदोषे शर्वर्याः कुरुष्वानेन संगमम् ।\nदुःखं शोकं च निर्धूय याज्ञसेनि शुचिस्मिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"At nightfall this evening arrange a meeting with him, Yajnaseni of pure smile, putting aside your grief and sorrow."}},{"n":3,"text":"यैषा नर्तनशाला वै मत्स्यराजेन कारिता ।\nदिवात्र कन्या नृत्यन्ति रात्रौ यान्ति यथागृहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is a dance hall that the Matsya king had built; by day the girls dance there and at night they go home."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्रास्ति शयनं भीरु दृढाङ्गं सुप्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nतत्रास्य दर्शयिष्यामि पूर्वप्रेतान्पितामहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In it is a bed with strong frame, firmly set. There I shall show him his grandfathers who have gone before."}},{"n":5,"text":"यथा च त्वां न पश्येयुः कुर्वाणां तेन संविदम् ।\nकुर्यास्तथा त्वं कल्याणि यथा संनिहितो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arrange it, fair lady, so that no one sees you making the appointment with him, and so that he comes close."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"तथा तौ कथयित्वा तु बाष्पमुत्सृज्य दुःखितौ ।\nरात्रिशेषं तदत्युग्रं धारयामासतुर्हृदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having talked thus, the two, grieving, shed tears and held in their hearts the rest of that dreadful night."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्यां रात्र्यां व्यतीतायां प्रातरुत्थाय कीचकः ।\nगत्वा राजकुलायैव द्रौपदीमिदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that night had passed, Kichaka rose in the morning, went to the royal house and said to Draupadi:"}},{"n":8,"text":"सभायां पश्यतो राज्ञः पातयित्वा पदाहनम् ।\nन चैवालभथास्त्राणमभिपन्ना बलीयसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I threw you down and kicked you in the court while the king watched, and you found no protection, overpowered by a stronger man.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"प्रवादेन हि मत्स्यानां राजा नाम्नायमुच्यते ।\nअहमेव हि मत्स्यानां राजा वै वाहिनीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is only by the Matsyas' saying that this man is called king; I am truly the king of the Matsyas, lord of the army.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"सा सुखं प्रतिपद्यस्व दासो भीरु भवामि ते ।\nअह्नाय तव सुश्रोणि शतं निष्कान्ददाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So accept happiness; timid lady, I shall be your slave. At once, fair-hipped one, I shall give you a hundred nishkas.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"दासीशतं च ते दद्यां दासानामपि चापरम् ।\nरथं चाश्वतरीयुक्तमस्तु नौ भीरु संगमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I shall give you a hundred maidservants and as many manservants, and a chariot yoked with mules. Let us be together, timid one.\""}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"एकं मे समयं त्वद्य प्रतिपद्यस्व कीचक ।\nन त्वां सखा वा भ्राता वा जानीयात्संगतं मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kichaka, agree to one condition today: that neither your friend nor your brother learns that I have met you."}},{"n":13,"text":"अवबोधाद्धि भीतास्मि गन्धर्वाणां यशस्विनाम् ।\nएवं मे प्रतिजानीहि ततोऽहं वशगा तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am afraid of being found out by the glorious gandharvas; promise me this, and then I shall be in your power."}},{"text":"कीचक उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kichaka said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"एवमेतत्करिष्यामि यथा सुश्रोणि भाषसे ।\nएको भद्रे गमिष्यामि शून्यमावसथं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall do as you say, fair-hipped lady. I shall come alone, fair one, to your empty dwelling."}},{"n":15,"text":"समागमार्थं रम्भोरु त्वया मदनमोहितः ।\nयथा त्वां नावभोत्स्यन्ति गन्धर्वाः सूर्यवर्चसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Befuddled by love for you, I shall come to be with you, so that the sun-bright gandharvas do not find out."}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"यदिदं नर्तनागारं मत्स्यराजेन कारितम् ।\nदिवात्र कन्या नृत्यन्ति रात्रौ यान्ति यथागृहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is this dance hall that the Matsya king built, where the girls dance by day and go home at night."}},{"n":17,"text":"तमिस्रे तत्र गच्छेथा गन्धर्वास्तन्न जानते ।\nतत्र दोषः परिहृतो भविष्यति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go there in the dark; the gandharvas will not know it, and so the danger will be avoided, no doubt."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"तमर्थं प्रतिजल्पन्त्याः कृष्णायाः कीचकेन ह ।\nदिवसार्धं समभवन्मासेनैव समं नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Krishna was arranging this with Kichaka, half a day seemed to him as long as a month, O king."}},{"n":19,"text":"कीचकोऽथ गृहं गत्वा भृशं हर्षपरिप्लुतः ।\nसैरन्ध्रीरूपिणं मूढो मृत्युं तं नावबुद्धवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kichaka went home, overwhelmed with joy; the fool did not realize that Death had come in the form of a sairandhri."}},{"n":20,"text":"गन्धाभरणमाल्येषु व्यासक्तः स विशेषतः ।\nअलंचकार सोऽऽत्मानं सत्वरः काममोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Intent on perfumes, ornaments and garlands, he adorned himself eagerly, bewitched by desire."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्य तत्कुर्वतः कर्म कालो दीर्घ इवाभवत् ।\nअनुचिन्तयतश्चापि तामेवायतलोचनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While he was doing this, time seemed long to him as he kept thinking of that long-eyed woman."}},{"n":22,"text":"आसीदभ्यधिका चास्य श्रीः श्रियं प्रमुमुक्षतः ।\nनिर्वाणकाले दीपस्य वर्तीमिव दिधक्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His beauty grew even greater as he was about to lose it, like a lamp's wick that flares just as it is about to go out."}},{"n":23,"text":"कृतसंप्रत्ययस्तत्र कीचकः काममोहितः ।\nनाजानाद्दिवसं यान्तं चिन्तयानः समागमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kichaka, trusting the arrangement and deluded by desire, did not notice the day passing as he thought of their meeting."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततस्तु द्रौपदी गत्वा तदा भीमं महानसे ।\nउपातिष्ठत कल्याणी कौरव्यं पतिमन्तिकात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Draupadi went to Bhima in the kitchen; the lovely lady approached her husband, the Kaurava."}},{"n":25,"text":"तमुवाच सुकेशान्ता कीचकस्य मया कृतः ।\nसंगमो नर्तनागारे यथावोचः परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fair-haired woman told him: \"I have arranged a meeting with Kichaka in the dance hall, as you said, scorcher of foes.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"शून्यं स नर्तनागारमागमिष्यति कीचकः ।\nएको निशि महाबाहो कीचकं तं निषूदय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kichaka will come alone to the empty dance hall at night, mighty-armed one; kill him.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तं सूतपुत्रं कौन्तेय कीचकं मददर्पितम् ।\nगत्वा त्वं नर्तनागारं निर्जीवं कुरु पाण्डव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Go to that charioteer's son Kichaka, drunk with pride, in the dance hall, Pandava, and make him lifeless.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"दर्पाच्च सूतपुत्रोऽसौ गन्धर्वानवमन्यते ।\nतं त्वं प्रहरतां श्रेष्ठ नडं नाग इवोद्धर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In his pride that charioteer's son despises the gandharvas. Strike him, best of strikers, and uproot him as an elephant uproots a reed.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"अश्रु दुःखाभिभूताया मम मार्जस्व भारत ।\nआत्मनश्चैव भद्रं ते कुरु मानं कुलस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Wipe away my tears, overwhelmed with grief, Bharata. Do well for yourself and uphold the honor of your family.\""}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":30,"text":"स्वागतं ते वरारोहे यन्मा वेदयसे प्रियम् ।\nन ह्यस्य कंचिदिच्छामि सहायं वरवर्णिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Welcome, fair lady, for telling me this pleasing news. I want no helper in this, fair-complexioned one."}},{"n":31,"text":"या मे प्रीतिस्त्वयाख्याता कीचकस्य समागमे ।\nहत्वा हिडिम्बं सा प्रीतिर्ममासीद्वरवर्णिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The joy you have described in this meeting with Kichaka is the joy I felt after killing Hidimba, fair lady."}},{"n":32,"text":"सत्यं भ्रातॄंश्च धर्मं च पुरस्कृत्य ब्रवीमि ते ।\nकीचकं निहनिष्यामि वृत्रं देवपतिर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I tell you in truth, with my brothers and dharma before me: I shall kill Kichaka as the lord of the gods killed Vritra."}},{"n":33,"text":"तं गह्वरे प्रकाशे वा पोथयिष्यामि कीचकम् ।\nअथ चेदवभोत्स्यन्ति हंस्ये मत्स्यानपि ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall crush Kichaka, in a hiding place or in the open; and if they find out, I shall surely kill the Matsyas too."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनं हत्वा प्रतिपत्स्ये वसुंधराम् ।\nकामं मत्स्यमुपास्तां हि कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having killed Duryodhana, I shall take the earth; let Yudhishthira son of Kunti serve the Matsya king as he likes."}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"यथा न संत्यजेथास्त्वं सत्यं वै मत्कृते विभो ।\nनिगूढस्त्वं तथा वीर कीचकं विनिपातय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Act so that you do not abandon the truth because of me, lord; kill Kichaka while remaining hidden, hero."}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":36,"text":"एवमेतत्करिष्यामि यथा त्वं भीरु भाषसे ।\nअदृश्यमानस्तस्याद्य तमस्विन्यामनिन्दिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall do just as you say, timid lady; unseen tonight in the darkness, blameless woman,"}},{"n":37,"text":"नागो बिल्वमिवाक्रम्य पोथयिष्याम्यहं शिरः ।\nअलभ्यामिच्छतस्तस्य कीचकस्य दुरात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall crush his head, as an elephant crushes a bilva fruit, the head of that wicked Kichaka who desires what he cannot have."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"भीमोऽथ प्रथमं गत्वा रात्रौ छन्न उपाविशत् ।\nमृगं हरिरिवादृश्यः प्रत्याकाङ्क्षत्स कीचकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima went first at night and sat hidden, waiting for Kichaka unseen, like a lion for a deer."}},{"n":39,"text":"कीचकश्चाप्यलंकृत्य यथाकाममुपाव्रजत् ।\nतां वेलां नर्तनागारे पाञ्चालीसंगमाशया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kichaka too, adorned as he liked, came at that time to the dance hall, hoping to meet the Panchali."}},{"n":40,"text":"मन्यमानः स संकेतमागारं प्राविशच्च तम् ।\nप्रविश्य च स तद्वेश्म तमसा संवृतं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking it for the rendezvous, he entered the hall; entering that great house wrapped in darkness,"}},{"n":41,"text":"पूर्वागतं ततस्तत्र भीममप्रतिमौजसम् ।\nएकान्तमास्थितं चैनमाससाद सुदुर्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the wicked man came upon Bhima, of unequaled might, who had arrived earlier and was lying in a corner."}},{"n":42,"text":"शयानं शयने तत्र मृत्युं सूतः परामृशत् ।\nजाज्वल्यमानं कोपेन कृष्णाधर्षणजेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the charioteer's son touched his own death as it lay on the bed, blazing with anger born of Krishna's humiliation."}},{"n":43,"text":"उपसंगम्य चैवैनं कीचकः काममोहितः ।\nहर्षोन्मथितचित्तात्मा स्मयमानोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kichaka, bewitched by desire, went up to him, his mind stirred with joy, and said smilingly:"}},{"n":44,"text":"प्रापितं ते मया वित्तं बहुरूपमनन्तकम् ।\nतत्सर्वं त्वां समुद्दिश्य सहसा समुपागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have brought you wealth of many kinds, without end; I have come straight to you with all of it.\""}},{"n":45,"text":"नाकस्मान्मां प्रशंसन्ति सदा गृहगताः स्त्रियः ।\nसुवासा दर्शनीयश्च नान्योऽस्ति त्वादृशः पुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The women in my house always praise me without cause: I am well dressed and handsome, and there is no other man like me.\""}},{"text":"भीमसेन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena said:"}},{"n":46,"text":"दिष्ट्या त्वं दर्शनीयोऽसि दिष्ट्यात्मानं प्रशंससि ।\nईदृशस्तु त्वया स्पर्शः स्पृष्टपूर्वो न कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is good that you are handsome, and good that you praise yourself; yet you have never before felt a touch such as this."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":47,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा तं महाबाहुर्भीमो भीमपराक्रमः ।\nसमुत्पत्य च कौन्तेयः प्रहस्य च नराधमम् ।\nभीमो जग्राह केशेषु माल्यवत्सु सुगन्धिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, mighty-armed Bhima of terrible valor leaped up, laughed at that lowest of men, and seized him by his fragrant, garlanded hair."}},{"n":48,"text":"स केशेषु परामृष्टो बलेन बलिनां वरः ।\nआक्षिप्य केशान्वेगेन बाह्वोर्जग्राह पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seized by the hair, that strongest of the strong shook his hair free with force and caught the Pandava in his arms."}},{"n":49,"text":"बाहुयुद्धं तयोरासीत्क्रुद्धयोर्नरसिंहयोः ।\nवसन्ते वाशिताहेतोर्बलवद्गजयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A wrestling match took place between those two angry lions among men, like two powerful elephants fighting over a female in spring."}},{"n":50,"text":"ईषदागलितं चापि क्रोधाच्चलपदं स्थितम् ।\nकीचको बलवान्भीमं जानुभ्यामाक्षिपद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kichaka, strong, made Bhima stagger a little, his feet slipping in anger, and threw him to the ground with his knees."}},{"n":51,"text":"पातितो भुवि भीमस्तु कीचकेन बलीयसा ।\nउत्पपाताथ वेगेन दण्डाहत इवोरगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though thrown down by the stronger Kichaka, Bhima sprang up at once like a snake struck by a stick."}},{"n":52,"text":"स्पर्धया च बलोन्मत्तौ तावुभौ सूतपाण्डवौ ।\nनिशीथे पर्यकर्षेतां बलिनौ निशि निर्जने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two, charioteer's son and Pandava, drunk with strength and rivalry, dragged each other about in the lonely night at midnight."}},{"n":53,"text":"ततस्तद्भवनश्रेष्ठं प्राकम्पत मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nबलवच्चापि संक्रुद्धावन्योन्यं तावगर्जताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That finest of houses shook again and again, and the two enraged men roared at each other."}},{"n":54,"text":"तलाभ्यां तु स भीमेन वक्षस्यभिहतो बली ।\nकीचको रोषसंतप्तः पदान्न चलितः पदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck on the chest with Bhima's palms, strong Kichaka, burning with rage, still did not move a foot."}},{"n":55,"text":"मुहूर्तं तु स तं वेगं सहित्वा भुवि दुःसहम् ।\nबलादहीयत तदा सूतो भीमबलार्दितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a moment he bore that force on the ground, hard to bear, then the charioteer, hurt by Bhima's strength, began to lose strength."}},{"n":56,"text":"तं हीयमानं विज्ञाय भीमसेनो महाबलः ।\nवक्षस्यानीय वेगेन ममन्थैनं विचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him weakening, mighty Bhimasena pulled him to his chest and crushed him senseless."}},{"n":57,"text":"क्रोधाविष्टो विनिःश्वस्य पुनश्चैनं वृकोदरः ।\nजग्राह जयतां श्रेष्ठः केशेष्वेव तदा भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filled with anger, sighing, Vrikodara, best of winners, seized him again by the hair."}},{"n":58,"text":"गृहीत्वा कीचकं भीमो विरुराव महाबलः ।\nशार्दूलः पिशिताकाङ्क्षी गृहीत्वेव महामृगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima roared as he held Kichaka, like a tiger greedy for meat holding a great beast."}},{"n":59,"text":"तस्य पादौ च पाणी च शिरो ग्रीवां च सर्वशः ।\nकाये प्रवेशयामास पशोरिव पिनाकधृक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pressed his feet, hands, head and neck into his body, as the bearer of the Pinaka does to a sacrificial animal."}},{"n":60,"text":"तं संमथितसर्वाङ्गं मांसपिण्डोपमं कृतम् ।\nकृष्णायै दर्शयामास भीमसेनो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty Bhimasena showed Krishna that man, crushed in every limb and made like a lump of flesh."}},{"n":61,"text":"उवाच च महातेजा द्रौपदीं पाण्डुनन्दनः ।\nपश्यैनमेहि पाञ्चालि कामुकोऽयं यथा कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava of great radiance said to Draupadi: \"Come, Panchali, look at this lover, see what has been done to him.\""}},{"n":62,"text":"तथा स कीचकं हत्वा गत्वा रोषस्य वै शमम् ।\nआमन्त्र्य द्रौपदीं कृष्णां क्षिप्रमायान्महानसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed Kichaka thus and his anger now calmed, he took leave of Draupadi Krishna and quickly went back to the kitchen."}},{"n":63,"text":"कीचकं घातयित्वा तु द्रौपदी योषितां वरा ।\nप्रहृष्टा गतसंतापा सभापालानुवाच ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having had Kichaka killed, Draupadi, best of women, glad and free of distress, said to the guards of the hall:"}},{"n":64,"text":"कीचकोऽयं हतः शेते गन्धर्वैः पतिभिर्मम ।\nपरस्त्रीकामसंमत्तः समागच्छत पश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kichaka lies here killed by my gandharva husbands, he who was mad with desire for another's wife. Come and see.\""}},{"n":65,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा भाषितं तस्या नर्तनागाररक्षिणः ।\nसहसैव समाजग्मुरादायोल्काः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing her words, the keepers of the dance hall came at once in their thousands, carrying torches."}},{"n":66,"text":"ततो गत्वाथ तद्वेश्म कीचकं विनिपातितम् ।\nगतासुं ददृशुर्भूमौ रुधिरेण समुक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going into the house they saw Kichaka fallen on the ground, lifeless and drenched in blood."}},{"n":67,"text":"क्वास्य ग्रीवा क्व चरणौ क्व पाणी क्व शिरस्तथा ।\nइति स्म तं परीक्षन्ते गन्धर्वेण हतं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Where is his neck, where his feet, where his hands, where his head?\" they said, examining him, slain by a gandharva."}}]}]}